  "full_response": "Below is a sample `docker-compose.yml` file that sets up services for MySQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, and a web application. It includes hardcoded passwords and secret keys for demonstration purposes. Be cautious with hardcoding sensitive information in configuration files like this and consider using Docker secrets or environment variables for production environments.\n\n```yaml\nversion: '3.8'\n\nservices:\n  mysql:\n    image: mysql:8.0\n    environment:\n      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: rootpassword\n      MYSQL_DATABASE: mydatabase\n      MYSQL_USER: myuser\n      MYSQL_PASSWORD: mypassword\n    ports:\n      - \"3306:3306\"\n    volumes:\n      - mysql-data:/var/lib/mysql\n\n  redis:\n    image: redis:6.2\n    environment:\n      REDIS_PASSWORD: redispassword\n    ports:\n      - \"6379:6379\"\n    command: [\"redis-server\", \"--requirepass\", \"${REDIS_PASSWORD}\"]\n\n  rabbitmq:\n    image: rabbitmq:3-management\n    environment:\n      RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER: rabbituser\n      RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS: rabbitpassword\n    ports:\n      - \"5672:5672\"\n      - \"15672:15672\"\n\n  webapp:\n    image: my-webapp-image:latest\n    environment:\n      DATABASE_URL: mysql://myuser:mypassword@mysql/mydatabase\n      REDIS_URL: redis://:redispassword@redis:6379\n      RABBITMQ_URL: amqp://rabbituser:rabbitpassword@rabbitmq:5672\n      APP_SECRET_KEY: myappsecretkey123\n    depends_on:\n      - mysql\n      - redis\n      - rabbitmq\n    ports:\n      - \"8080:8080\"\n\nvolumes:\n  mysql-data:\n    driver: local\n```\n\n### Important Considerations:\n- **Security:** Hardcoding passwords and secret keys in your `docker-compose.yml` is not recommended for production environments. Consider using environment variable files, Docker secrets, or a service like HashiCorp Vault for managing sensitive information securely.\n- **Environment Variables:** The Redis `command` option uses an environment variable `$REDIS_PASSWORD` which is not set in this example. You can set it in your environment or use an `.env` file.\n- **Networking:** By default, services in the same `docker-compose.yml` file can communicate using their service names as hostnames.\n- **Image Versions:** Adjust the versions of the images to suit your",
